======== Leetcode 73. Set Matrix Zeroes ======
Step 1: Find the number of rows and columns in the matrix.
Step 2: Create one boolean array to track which rows should become zero.
Step 3: Create another boolean array to track which columns should become zero.
Step 4: Traverse the entire matrix using two loops (row by row, column by column).
Step 5: Whenever you find a cell that contains 0, mark that row index as true in the row array and mark that column index as true in the column array.
Step 6: After checking the whole matrix, you now know exactly which rows and columns must be set to zero.
Step 7: Traverse the matrix again.
Step 8: For each cell, check if its row is marked true or its column is marked true.
Step 9: If either the row or column is marked, set that cell value to 0.
Step 10: After completing this second traversal, the matrix will have all required rows and columns converted to zero.

Time Complexity: O(m × n)
Space Complexity: O(m + n)




             ---------------> Code <-----------------
class Solution {
    public void setZeroes(int[][] matrix) {
        int row=matrix.length;
        int col=matrix[0].length;

        boolean[] r=new boolean[row];
        boolean[] c=new boolean[col];

        for(int i=0;i<row;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<col;j++){
                if(matrix[i][j]==0){
                    r[i]=true;
                    c[j]=true;
                }
            }
        }

        for(int i=0;i<row;i++){
            for(int j=0;j<col;j++){
                if(r[i] || c[j]){
                    matrix[i][j]=0;
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
